12
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:28,880
Propanoic acid is weak.

13
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:31,600
At any moment only a small fraction of

14
00:00:31,680 --> 00:00:34,240
its molecules have given a proton to water,

15
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:37,120
and the rest stay whole, so the hydronium

16
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:39,680
is far less than the acid's concentration.

17
00:00:40,320 --> 00:00:43,360
Molecules and ions sit in equilibrium, and you've

18
00:00:43,520 --> 00:00:46,800
already written its constant, K a: hydronium times

19
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:49,680
propanoate, over the whole acid, with water left

20
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:50,640
out.

21
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:52,560
So the real question is how much of

22
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:54,560
the acid ionises.

23
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:56,080
Call that amount x.

24
00:00:57,300 --> 00:00:59,780
Here's the full method, with K a for

25
00:00:59,860 --> 00:01:02,500
propanoic acid one point three times ten to

26
00:01:02,580 --> 00:01:03,540
the minus five.

27
00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:08,020
An ICE table tracks the concentrations: initial, change,

28
00:01:08,140 --> 00:01:08,980
equilibrium.

29
00:01:09,220 --> 00:01:11,620
At the start there's zero point one five

30
00:01:11,740 --> 00:01:14,340
zero of the acid and, ignoring water's own

31
00:01:14,420 --> 00:01:16,540
tiny share, no ions.

32
00:01:16,740 --> 00:01:19,860
Each molecule that ionises makes one hydronium and

33
00:01:19,940 --> 00:01:22,740
one propanoate, so the acid goes down by

34
00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:25,660
x and each ion goes up by x.

35
00:01:25,860 --> 00:01:28,820
At equilibrium, that's zero point one five zero

36
00:01:28,980 --> 00:01:31,700
minus x, then x, and x.

37
00:01:31,940 --> 00:01:34,420
So K a equals x squared over zero

38
00:01:34,580 --> 00:01:36,820
point one five zero minus x.

39
00:01:38,034 --> 00:01:40,401
K a is tiny next to zero point

40
00:01:40,434 --> 00:01:41,393
one five zero,

41
00:01:41,914 --> 00:01:43,393
so x is tiny too.

42
00:01:43,954 --> 00:01:46,353
Taking a tiny amount from zero point one

43
00:01:46,514 --> 00:01:49,233
five zero still leaves about zero point one

44
00:01:49,314 --> 00:01:51,393
five zero, so we drop the x from

45
00:01:51,434 --> 00:01:53,793
the bottom, just like the tiny K shortcut

46
00:01:53,874 --> 00:01:55,113
